    <blockquote>"I work with our early learners, and the row view changed how I teach. I used to dig through folders for notes, figure out when a child last came and what they were struggling with, and scribble reminders on sticky notes before they left. Now each child's card shows the notes from past sessions, a checklist and flags for exactly what they need that day, and a timer that warns me when they are down to their last five minutes. I add notes and record test results right there, and it all saves to their record. When the owner preps for a progress meeting, it is already in the system, not in my memory. <strong>I get to actually teach.</strong>"</blockquote>
